  "markscheme": {
    "html": "<p>C</p>\n<p>The insulated cylinder implies an adiabatic compression (Q=0). The work done on the gas is W = Fd = 500 N × 0.10 m = 50 J. From the first law of thermodynamics, the internal energy increases by ΔU = W = 50 J. Assuming the ideal gas is monatomic, its internal energy change is ΔU = (3/2)nRΔT. With n=1 mol and R=8.31 J K⁻¹ mol⁻¹, the temperature change is ΔT = ΔU / ((3/2)R) ≈ 4 K. The final temperature is thus 80 °C + 4 °C = 84 °C.</p>"
  },
  "paper": "paper_1a",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>One mole of an ideal gas is enclosed in an insulated cylinder. The temperature of the gas is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"80^\\circ\\mathrm{C}\"></span>. A piston is then pushed with a force of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"500\\,\\mathrm{N}\"></span> over a distance of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"10\\,\\mathrm{cm}\"></span> to compress the gas.</p>\n<p>What is the final temperature?</p>\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure>\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_02\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 2\" src=\"asset:fig_02\"/></figure>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"> <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"480^\\circ\\mathrm{C}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"> <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"400^\\circ\\mathrm{C}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"> <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"84^\\circ\\mathrm{C}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"> <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4^\\circ\\mathrm{C}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
